function pNotes(){return card("Data notes for Bannu Division","What the underlying data does and does not contain",`<ul class="svn"><li><b>AFP cases and lab results.</b> EDCS line list for the three districts, onset 2022 to date. Cases are placed in a union council by UC code, then by UC name.</li><li><b>Population.</b> Under-15 population is estimated from the campaign target of children under five (under five = 17% of population, under 15 = 45%), so NPAFP, true AFP and GBS rates are estimates.</li><li><b>Spot maps.</b> The line list has no case coordinates, so case and active site spots are placed at random inside the union council.</li><li><b>Laboratory.</b> Isolation is counted per AFP case from the final result in the line list. Contact specimens are not in the data supplied.</li><li><b>Environmental surveillance.</b> Five regular sites from the reviewed June 2026 site list; other sampling sites are listed under other ES sampling.</li><li><b>Active site visits.</b> 57 assigned active sites checked against the 26 Nov 2026 visit export, complete weeks to week 46, fortnights to weeks 45-46 and months to October.</li><li><b>Zero-reporting sites.</b> No list supplied, so the zero site pages are empty.</li><li><b>Global update.</b> Taken from the GPEI update of 18 Nov 2026 (same as the Kohat Division dashboard).</li></ul>`)+card("How the indicators are calculated","",`<ul class="svn"><li><b>NPAFP rate.</b> AFP cases with final classification 3 (non-polio AFP), per 100,000 children under 15. The current year is annualised: cases to date \u00d7 365 \u00f7 days elapsed. Benchmark 3 per 100,000.</li><li><b>True AFP rate.</b> Cases whose provisional diagnosis is G61.0, G37.3, B34.1 or T80, per 100,000 children under 15.</li><li><b>GBS rate.</b> Provisional diagnosis G61 or GBS, per 100,000 under 15.</li><li><b>Stool adequacy.</b> AFP cases marked ADEQ, % of cases with an adequacy recorded. Benchmark 80%.</li><li><b>Notified within 7 days.</b> Date of notification minus date of onset is 0 to 7 days. Benchmark 80%.</li><li><b>Investigated within 48 hours.</b> Date of investigation minus date of notification is 0 to 2 days. Benchmark 90%.</li><li><b>NPEV and Sabin-like isolation.</b> Counted per stool specimen from the lab file (AFP cases and contacts). NPEV = enterovirus result 1. Sabin-like = poliovirus type 1, 2 or 3 result 2. Benchmark for NPEV 10%.</li><li><b>Environmental surveillance.</b> Results of ES samples from the regular ES sites in the national ES file (Hinjal and Noorabad, Muslim Abad Sokari, Tube Well Gali, Nala Serai Naurang and Miran Shah Town). A sample is NPEV positive when NPEV was isolated, Sabin-like positive when any Sabin-like poliovirus was isolated. ES NPEV benchmark: at least 50% of samples.</li><li><b>Active site visits.</b> Weekly, fortnightly and monthly active sites are checked against the 2026 visit trackers. A visit is met when the site was visited at least once in the period it was due. Green is 90% or more.</li><li><b>Population.</b> Under-15 population by district and tehsil from the indicator workbook. District totals use the district figures, tehsil rows use the tehsil figures.</li><li><b>Dates.</b> Cases are grouped by year and month of paralysis onset. Data is as of ${asof().toLocaleDateString("en-GB",{day:"numeric",month:"long",year:"numeric"})}, the latest entry in the AFP file.</li></ul>`)+card("Data sources","",`<p class="svs">EDCS AFP line list (Khyber Pakhtunkhwa), filtered to Bannu, Lakki Marwat and Wazir-N (North Waziristan), onset 2022 to 2026, the national ES results file, the reviewed ES site list (June 2026) and the 2026 active site visit trackers. No names, addresses or exact dates of birth are held in this dashboard.</p>`)}

